1
00:00:03,136 --> 00:00:06,276
(Sheldon:)I've invented a science joke,
would you like to hear it?

2
00:00:06,273 --> 00:00:07,943
(Amy:)Sure.

3
00:00:07,942 --> 00:00:11,542
(Sheldon:)How many Edisons does it take
to screw in a light bulb?

4
00:00:11,545 --> 00:00:13,215
(Amy:)How many?

5
00:00:13,214 --> 00:00:15,214
(Sheldon:)Who cares?
He stole the idea

6
00:00:15,216 --> 00:00:17,546
(Sheldon:)and doesn't deserve
his own joke.

7
00:00:17,551 --> 00:00:19,121
(Amy:)Is that really true?

8
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:21,790
(Sheldon:)Of course, that's how you know
it's a good joke.

9
00:00:21,789 --> 00:00:24,489
(Sheldon:)It not only entertains,
it informs.

10
00:00:25,893 --> 00:00:27,463
Hey, sorry
to interrupt.

11
00:00:27,461 --> 00:00:28,791
(Sheldon:)Uh, Barry,

12
00:00:28,796 --> 00:00:31,996
(Sheldon:)uh, how many Edisons does it
take to screw in a light bulb?

13
00:00:31,999 --> 00:00:34,469
(Barry:)Did you know Edison didn't
actually invent the light bulb?

14
00:00:37,638 --> 00:00:39,968
(Sheldon:)What do you want,
Barry?

15
00:00:39,974 --> 00:00:42,974
Just wanted to drop this off
as a little thank you for Amy.

16
00:00:42,977 --> 00:00:44,307
(Amy:)What's this for?

17
00:00:44,311 --> 00:00:46,111
Your idea really
helped me out.

18
00:00:46,113 --> 00:00:48,743
My light-cone quantization
paper's online already.

19
00:00:48,749 --> 00:00:51,249
The response
has been amazing.

20
00:00:51,252 --> 00:00:52,682
(Amy:)Well, that's
fascinating.

21
00:00:52,686 --> 00:00:54,156
(Amy:)I can't wait to read it.

22
00:00:54,155 --> 00:00:55,485
(Sheldon:)Oh, no, me as well.

23
00:00:55,489 --> 00:00:59,659
(Sheldon:)Uh, please e-mail it
to Sheldon@Bazinga.biz.

24
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:00,990
Why "dot-biz"?

25
00:01:00,995 --> 00:01:03,025
(Sheldon:)Because I just gave
you the business.

